  "prefLabel": "Rev 1501.18 Total capital structure",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rev 1501.18 “Total capital structure” means the specific mixture of long term debt and equity that a company uses to finance its operations that directly affects the risk and value of the business such as, but not limited to;\n\n(a) Long-term debt;\n\n(b) Preferred stock;\n\n(c) Common equity;\n\n(d) Current liabilities; and\n\n(e) Total capital.\n\nSource. #10662, eff 8-27-14; ss by #13977, eff 5-23-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/rev1500.html"
}
